   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Before",
     "texto": [
      "To say «before…», **-기 전에** is used: 자다 → **자기 전에** (before going to sleep), 먹다 → **먹기 전에** (before eating). A noun can also be used with **전에**: 수업 전에 = before class. The main action can be in the present, past, future or imperative, depending on what you want to say."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "After",
     "texto": [
      "To express that one action happens after another, **-(으)ㄴ 후에** is very commonly used: 먹다 → **먹은 후에** (after eating), 일어나다 → **일어난 후에** (after getting up). The ending -(으)ㄴ forms the modifier of the earlier action; it does not require the main sentence to be in the past: **일어난 후에 운동해요** = I exercise after getting up; **먹은 후에 쉬세요** = please rest after eating."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
